{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Calibrate Stage Centre}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 4YI0_82}
\pard\keepn {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Add}
\b\fs36\cf1 Calibrate Stage Centre
\par \pard \plain\fs24 It is a pre-requisite for all compucentric functions that the centre of the stage rotation is accurately known.
\par 
\par This will normally only need to be performed once each time the stage is serviced. However to achieve the ultimate accuracy it may be necessary to recalibrate the rotation centre each time the stage is initialised.
\par 
\par This dialog provides the Calibrate Stage Centre Wizard.
\par 
\par Instructions are displayed describing the operator actions required.
\par Press \b Next\plain\fs24  when the action is completed.
\par \pard Press \b Back\plain\fs24  button to return to the previous step.
\par Press \b Cancel\plain\fs24  to abort the sequence - stage will return to original position.
\par Press \b OK\plain\fs24  to accept the currently computed centre position at any point in the iteration.
\par 
\par The sequence is described below. 
\par Entries labeled STEP are operator actions, those labeled NEXT are the wizard actions taken when \b Next\plain\fs24  is pressed
\par 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b Step 1 \plain\fs24 Insert a suitable sample (e.g. calibration grid) into a single stub holder. The sample must be mounted centrally on the stub.
\par \tab \tab Optionally switch on backlash correction.
\par \tab \tab It is possible at this point to manually enter the Co-ordinates of the Rotation Centre and click \b OK\plain\fs24 
\par \b Next\tab \plain\fs24 Save stage position.
\par \pard\li1075\fi-355\tx1075 Move the stage to previously saved calibrated position or to nominal centre of stage travel. 
\par Magnification set to 30 X. 
\par Crosshairs On\b 
\par \pard\tx1075 \plain\fs24 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b Step 2\plain\fs24  Using \b Centre Point \plain\fs24 (Ctrl Tab) or the joystick position a distinguishable mark at centre screen
\par \pard\li1075\fi-355\tx1075 If required the \b Load Defaults \plain\fs24 button may be used to position the stage at the default centre of rotation for the current stage type.
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b Next\plain\fs24 \tab The stage is moved back to it's position at the start of step 2
\par 
\par \pard\tx355 \b Step3\plain\fs24  Instructs the user to watch the mark movement
\par \pard\tx355 \b Next\plain\fs24 \tab Rotates the stage by 180 degrees
\par 
\par \b Step 4\plain\fs24  Using \b Centre Point \plain\fs24 (Ctrl Tab) or the joystick position a distinguishable mark at centre screen
\par \b Next\plain\fs24 \tab The new centre position is computed.
\par 
\par \b Step 5\plain\fs24  At this point you must decide if the calibration is sufficiently accurate (press \b OK\plain\fs24 ) or if cycle is to be repeated at a higher magnification (press \b Next\plain\fs24 )
\par 
\par \b Next\plain\fs24 \tab Stage is moved to newly computed centre position
\par \pard\li1075\fi-355\tx1075 Magnification is increased
\par Go To Step 2
\par \pard\tx355 \b OK\plain\fs24  \tab Save new calibrated centre position.
\par \pard\li1075\fi-355\tx1075 Crosshairs off
\par Move stage to original position
\par \pard\tx1075 
\par \pard\tx1075 See also
\par \pard\tx1075 \uldb Stage Control Tab\plain\fs24 {\v KH.ZCT@tabmgr.hlp}
\par \pard\tx1075 \uldb Compucentric Stage Control\plain\fs24 {\v 10F6FNP@stage.hlp}
\par \pard\tx1075 \uldb Compucentric setup\plain\fs24 {\v 4YI0_83}
\par \pard\tx1075 \uldb Horizontal Stage Alignment\plain\fs24 {\v 4YI0_84}
\par \page
