\pard\keepn {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Beam Current Measurement}
\b\fs36\cf1 Compucentric Setup (Sample Height)
\par \pard \plain\fs24 It is a pre-requisite for compucentric tilt that the sample height (surface of sample relative to point of tilt rotation) is accurately known.
\par 
\par This will  need to be performed when the sample is changed.
\par 
\par This dialog provides the Calibrate Sample Height Wizard (Centre of Stage Rotation Calibration must have already been performed).
\par 
\par The first part of the calibration (steps 1 - 7) compute a sample height based on a 2 degree tilt. This is used in steps 8 onward to perform a more accurate calibration of the height for increasing tilt angles.
\par \pard You may terminate the calibration at the maximum tilt angle you will be using.
\par 
\par Instructions are displayed describing the operator actions required.
\par Press \b Next\plain\fs24  when the action is completed.
\par Press \b Back\plain\fs24  button to return to the previous step.
\par Press \b Cancel\plain\fs24  to abort the sequence - stage will return to original position.
\par Press \b OK\plain\fs24  to accept the currently computed Height.
\par 
\par The sequence is described below. 
\par Entries labeled STEP are operator actions, those labeled NEXT are the wizard actions taken when \b Next\plain\fs24  is pressed
\par \pard 
\par \b NOTE 1: How to centre the feature in steps 2 and 3.\plain\fs24 
\par Centre point is restricted to move the stage in X direction only.
\par If joystick is used you must move in X (horizonal) direction only.
\par To achieve Y positioning use the stage rotation.
\par 
\par \b NOTE 2: How to centre the feature in steps 5 and 6\plain\fs24 
\par Centre point is restricted to move the stage in the Y direction only.
\par If joystick is used you must move in the Y (vertical) direction only.
\par Ignore X positioning at this time.
\par \pard 
\par \b Note 3: How to centre the feature in steps 8 onwards\plain\fs24 
\par Centre point is restricted to move the stage in the Y direction only.
\par If joystick is used you must move in the Y (vertical) direction only.
\par X positioning may be adjusted by using the Tilt error scroll bar
\par 
\par 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b Step 1\plain\fs24  If required the sample height may be entered manually and \b OK\plain\fs24  clicked
\par \pard\tx355 \b Next\plain\fs24  \tab The Stage is moved to the centre of rotation (Y axis only)  and the tilt set to zero degrees
\par \pard\li1075\fi-355\tx1075 Magnification is set to 30X
\par \pard\tx1075 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b Step 2 \plain\fs24 Select a point on the X axis (horizontal centre line). 
\par \pard\li1075\fi-355\tx1075 Centre the selected point See Note 1 above
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b Next\plain\fs24  \tab Magnification is increased to 500X
\par 
\par \b Step 3\plain\fs24  Position the selected point more accurately.See Note 1 above
\par \b Next\plain\fs24 \tab Notify the user that stage will be tilted
\par 
\par \b Step 4\plain\fs24  No action
\par \b Next\plain\fs24 \tab Tilt the Stage 2 degrees
\par \pard\li1075\fi-355\tx1075 Set Magnification to 30X
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 
\par \b Step 5\plain\fs24  Centre the point . N.B. adjust Y direction only. See note 2 above
\par \b Next\plain\fs24 \tab Set Magnification to 500X
\par 
\par \b Step 6\plain\fs24  Centre the point more accurately. N.B. adjust Y direction only. See note 2 above
\par \b Next\plain\fs24 \tab Compute the sample height
\par 
\par \b Step 7\plain\fs24  Press OK to terminate calibration here
\par \b Next\plain\fs24 \tab Perform Compucentric tilt of 8 degrees, Mag = 500X
\par 
\par \b Step 8\plain\fs24  Centre the feature. See Note 3 above
\par \b Next\plain\fs24 \tab Compute the sample height
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 
\par \b Step 9\plain\fs24  Press OK to terminate calibration here
\par \b Next\plain\fs24 \tab Perform Compucentric tilt of 15 degrees, Mag = 500X
\par 
\par \b Step 10\plain\fs24  Centre the feature. See Note 3 above.
\par \b Next\plain\fs24 \tab Compute the sample height
\par 
\par \b Step 11\plain\fs24  Press OK to terminate calibration here
\par \b Next\plain\fs24 \tab Perform Compucentric tilt of 30 degrees, Mag = 500X
\par 
\par \b Step 12\plain\fs24  Centre the feature. See Note 3 above.
\par \b Next\plain\fs24 \tab Compute the sample height
\par 
\par \b Step 13\plain\fs24  Press OK to terminate calibration here
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b Next\plain\fs24 \tab Perform Compucentric tilt of 45 degrees, Mag = 500X
\par 
\par \b Step 14\plain\fs24  Centre the feature. See Note 3 above.
\par \b Next\plain\fs24 \tab Compute the sample height
\par 
\par \b Step 15\plain\fs24  Press OK to finish
\par 
\par 
