\b\fs36\cf1 Input LUT Dialog
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par The Input\b  L\plain\fs24 ook \b U\plain\fs24 p \b T\plain\fs24 able (LUT) controls the transformation of the input signal before it reaches the store. Four different transformations can be applied:
\par 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx8495\cellx8995\cellx12615\pard\intbl \b Transparent:\plain\fs24 
\par\intbl The input LUT is set to linear so that the signal passes through the LUT unchanged.
\par\intbl \b Gamma:\plain\fs24 
\par\intbl \f13 Gamma correction changes the LUT relationship between the input signal and the output signal. It can be used to expand the contrast in an image if much of the image detail is contained in a small number of grey levels.
\par\intbl \f4 The input LUT is set according to the gamma parameter. Select the parameter with the \ul Scroll Bar\plain\fs24 {\v 2HOSDE@Sem.HLP} below. 
\par\intbl \b Inverse:\plain\fs24 
\par\intbl The input LUT is set to inverted linear so that the signal passes through the LUT with inverted contrast.
\par\intbl \b User:
\par\intbl \plain\fs24 Uses the user defined Input LUT.
\par\intbl \par\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm8.bmp\}\tab Select the mode by \ul clicking\plain\fs24 {\v CLICK@Sem.HLP} on one of the \ul Radio Buttons\plain\fs24 {\v 2R6X4F@Sem.HLP}\cell\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \pard\intbl\tx355 \par\pard \pard\intbl \cell\pard \pard\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm19.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard 
