{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Mounting of  Back Scattered Detector}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Mounting_of__Back_Scattered_Detector}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Mounting of  Back Scattered Detector
\par \pard \plain\fs24    
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx5665\cellx12685\pard\intbl The detector diode (1) is mounted underneath the final lens (2). The primary electron beam (PE) travels through the final lens and hits the specimen (3) where it releases back scattered electrons. These reach the detector (1) and generate an electrical signal there. 
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl The signal is taken out from the specimen chamber to the preamplifier (5) through the adjustment rod (4). The adjustment rod is used to slide the detector in and out.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl The adjustment of the 4 detector segments is done in the \uldb \b 4QBSD Control Panel\plain\b\fs24 {\v 4QBSD_Dialog}\plain\fs24  and brightness and contrast are adjusted from the \uldb \b Detectors SEM Control Panel\plain\b\fs24 {\v 1WE3854@TabMgr.HLP}\plain\fs24 .\cell\pard \pard\intbl 
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm24.wmf\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard 
\par \page
