{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Stage Horizontal alignment}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 4YI0_84}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Stage Horizontal alignment
\par \pard \plain\fs24 This Wizard is used to move the stage such that a linear feature on the sample, identified by two points, is horizontal with the second of the two points visible on screen.
\par 
\par The Stage Centre must be \uldb calibrated\plain\fs24 {\v 4YI0_82} for this function to be used.
\par 
\par Instructions are displayed describing the operator actions required.
\par Press \b Next\plain\fs24  when the action is completed.
\par Press \b Back\plain\fs24  button to return to the previous step.
\par Press \b Cancel\plain\fs24  to abort the sequence - stage will return to original position.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par The sequence is described below. 
\par Entries labeled STEP are operator actions, those labeled NEXT are the wizard actions taken when \b Next\plain\fs24  is pressed
\par 
\par \b Step 1\plain\fs24   Using \b Centre Point \plain\fs24 (Ctrl Tab), or the joystick, position the first point at centre screen
\par \b Next\plain\fs24 \tab Record the first stage position.
\par 
\par \b Step 2\plain\fs24   Using \b Centre Point \plain\fs24 (Ctrl Tab), or the joystick, position the sercond point at centre screen
\par \b Next\plain\fs24 \tab Compute the rotation required and perform compucentric rotation
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \b Finish\plain\fs24  Close the dialog
\par 
\par 
\par See also
\par \uldb Stage Control Tab\plain\fs24 {\v KH.ZCT@tabmgr.hlp}
\par \uldb Compucentric Stage Control\plain\fs24 {\v 10F6FNP@stage.hlp}
\par \uldb Calibrate stage centre of rotation\plain\fs24 {\v 4YI0_82}
\par \page
