{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} N6.C9U}
\pard \fs32\cf1 Static Stereo\b\fs36 
\par \plain\fs24 The Static Stereo function enables the user to combine two stored images to form a stereo image in the image store.
\par \f6 
\par \pard\li715 The left hand image of a static stereo image can be loaded into the image store.
\par This can be copied to the off screen area using the \b A to B\plain\f6\fs24  button.
\par The right hand image of a static stereo image can be loaded into the image store.
\par Press the \b Static Stereo\plain\f6\fs24  radio button to combine the two images.\f4 
\par \page
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 38VO_SM}
\pard \fs28\cf1 Semi Dynamic Stereo\b\fs36 
\par \plain\f6\fs24 The Semi Dynamic Stereo function enables the user to combine one stored image and one live image to form a stereo image in the image store. \b 
\par \pard\li715 
\par \plain\f6\fs24 Set the sample to one position, press the \b Semi Dyn. Stereo\plain\f6\fs24  radio button, this will freeze the blue portion of the Semi Dynamic Stereo image, leaving the red portion live.
\par Tilt the sample to produce a stereo effect.
\par \b 
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Static Stereo Depth Measurement}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Static_Stereo_Depth}
\pard \plain\fs32\cf1 Static Stereo Depth Measurement
\par \b\fs36 
\par \plain\f14\fs24 The depth of a point from the height of a reference point can be calculated by measuring the distance from the point of interest to a reference point on the tilt axis, tilting the sample and measuring the new distance from the point of interest to the reference point. The reference point must not move hence must be on the tilt axis.
\par 
\par Using the Point to Point Cursors place the P1R cursor and the P2R cursor on the reference point on the tilt axis.
\par \pard Place the P1 cursor on the point of interest.
\par Tilt the sample by a known number of degrees. The reference point should not move.
\par Place the P2 cursor on the point of interest (It should have moved ).  
\par The angle the sample has been tilted can be entered into the St. Stereo Angle parameter.
\par Press the Calc Static Stereo Depth button.
\par The  Respective depths as shown on the \ul diagram\plain\f14\fs24 {\v Static_Stereo_theory} are calculated.
\par \f4 
\par \fs20 
\par \page
