\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} 3 point alignment}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 3_point_alignment}
\pard \b\fs36\cf1 Three Point Alignment
\par \plain\fs24 If the 3 Point Alignment checkbox is ticked then 3 alignment points are used which permits the algorithm to handle different units in the X and Y direction
\par  (e.g. the X dimension may be a horizontal count of rectangular structures and the Y dimension a vertical count of the structures).
\par 
\par The first 2 points (User Co-ordinates X1, Y1 and X2, Y2) are as for 2 point alignment.
\par \{bmc bm46.bmp\}
\par The third point may be at X1, Y2 or at X2, Y1 as specified by the X2,Y1 checkbox.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Points list Text File Format}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Points_list_Text_File_Format}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Depth;Do Backlash;Edit Points Dialog;External Scan Control Dialog;Go To First;Go To Next;Go To Previous;Go To Selected;Hold Airlock Vacuum;Input LUT Dialog;Label Position;Load;Magnification Calibration Dialog}
\b\fs36\cf1 Points list Text File Format
\par \pard \plain\fs24 The stage points list may be saved /loaded as a text file, e.g. for importing into an Excel spreadsheet.
\par 
\par The data is in comma separated format as shown in the following example
\par 
\par Leo Points List
\par Absolute
\par Label,X,Y,Z,T,R,M,Mag,WD
\par 2
\par here,0.01000000,0.01000000,0.00000000,-1.00000000,0.00000000,0.00000000,100.000000,0.00500000
\par there,0.01500000,0.01500000,0.00500000,0.00000000,0.00000000,0.00000000,100.000000,0.00500000
\par 
\par 
\par Line 1 is fixed header \b Leo Points List \plain\fs24 to define type of data
\par \pard Line 2 is either \b Absolute\plain\fs24  or \b Relative\plain\fs24  (relative if stage registration is used)
\par Line 3 is column headings (content ignored on loading but line must be present)
\par Line 4 is count of point data entries which follow
\par 
\par X,Y,Z,M are positions in Metres.
\par T,R as positions in degrees.
\par Working distance is in Metres.
\par 
\par 
\par If preparing a file to be loaded please note that lines 1 through 4 are mandatory.
\par 
\par Example Importing into Excel:
\par  File saved as \b Example.TXT\plain\fs24 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \f7\b \{bmc bm8.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Start Excel\b 
\par \plain\f7\fs24 \{bmc bm8.bmp\}\f4\b \tab \plain\fs24 File Open
\par \f7 \{bmc bm8.bmp\}\f4 \tab Select file type = \b Text Files\plain\fs24 
\par \f7\b \{bmc bm8.bmp\}\plain\fs24 \tab Select File name = \b Example.TXT
\par \f7 \{bmc bm8.bmp\}\f4 \tab \plain\fs24 Select \b Delimited\plain\fs24  and \b Next
\par \f7 \{bmc bm8.bmp\}\f4 \tab \plain\fs24 Select \b Comma\plain\fs24  and \b Next
\par \plain\f7\fs24 \{bmc bm8.bmp\}\f4\b \tab \plain\fs24 Select \b General\plain\fs24  and \b Finish\plain\fs24 
\par 
\par Example Exporting from Excel
\par In Excel:
\par \f7 \{bmc bm8.bmp\}\f4 \tab Select Table including header information as described above (lines 1 through 4)
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \f7 \{bmc bm8.bmp\}\f4 \tab Select Menu item \b File - SaveAs\plain\fs24 
\par \f7 \{bmc bm8.bmp\}\f4 \tab Select SaveAs type \b CSV (comma delimited)\plain\fs24  and \b Save\plain\fs24  (e.g. Example.CSV)
\par 
\par 
\par \page
